+
+# Booking cancellation
+
+## Request
+
+Plans change, and customers ask us to cancel their bookings. Add `cancel(bookingId, at)` to the rental
+service. It cancels the booking at the time `at` and returns `{ bookingId, refund }`, the amount given back
+to the customer. A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment, and a booking can only be cancelled
+once.
+
+## School rules (requirements)
+
+- R1. Money is an integer number of euro cents.
+- R2. Times are UTC, written as ISO-8601 strings.
+- R4. The same item cannot be booked for overlapping periods. A cancelled booking does not count.
+- R5. Cancellation policy (task-001): a booking cancelled less than 24 hours before its start gets no
+  refund; otherwise the full amount is refunded.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- AC1. `cancel(bookingId, at)` returns `{ bookingId, refund }`. (R1)
+- AC2. A booking cancelled at least 24 hours before its start is refunded its full `total`. Exactly 24
+  hours before counts as in time. (R5)
+- AC3. A booking cancelled less than 24 hours before its start is refunded `0`. A cancellation at or after
+  the start is also refunded `0`. (R5)
+- AC4. `at` must be a valid ISO-8601 UTC timestamp; an invalid one is refused with an error. (R2)
+- AC5. `cancel` throws for an unknown `bookingId`. (task-001)
+- AC6. `cancel` throws when the booking was already cancelled: a booking can only be cancelled once.
+- AC7. After cancellation the item is free for the cancelled period: `book` for an overlapping period
+  succeeds, and `availability` lists the item. (R4)
+- AC8. Other bookings are unaffected by a cancellation. (R4)
+
+## Test plan
+
+Test first (red, then green). Each acceptance criterion has at least one happy-path test and one
+error-path or edge-path test. Tests cover the 24-hour boundary (exactly 24 hours, one hour short), a
+cancellation after the start, and the release of equipment. Tests are deterministic: `at` is passed in,
+no wall-clock time, no randomness, no external services.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Persistence across restarts.
+- Partial refunds, cancellation fees beyond R5, and refunds for hourly bookings under a different rule.
+- Cancelling a booking that is not yet known to the service (no booking-time record is kept).
+
+## Build record
+
+- Tests first: 11 new tests in `tests/rental.test.ts` (a `cancel` group: full refund at 24 hours or more,
+  exactly 24 hours, less than 24 hours, after the start, the discounted total, a non-timestamp and an
+  impossible date refused, an unknown booking, cancelling twice, release of the equipment, and other
+  bookings still holding theirs). Red before the change: 8 failing, 60 passing.
+- Implementation: `src/index.ts`. `cancel(bookingId, at)` returns `{ bookingId, refund }`. A stay now
+  records its booking id and total, and a `cancelled` flag; clashes ignore cancelled stays, so the
+  equipment is free again. The refund is the full total when `start - at` is at least 24 hours, else 0
+  (R5). `at` is parsed with the same date check as the periods, but accepts any time of day.
+- Result: `npm test` passes, 68 of 68 (57 existing and 11 new). Type-checking with `tsc` was not run: no
+  TypeScript compiler is installed in this repository.
+- Choices made: a cancellation at or after the start is allowed and refunds 0, as R5 says "less than 24
+  hours before its start"; a cancelled booking is kept in the service, so a second cancel is refused
+  rather than reported as unknown; `at` is not checked against any booking-time record, since none is kept.
+  Cancellation of an hourly booking uses the same rule as a day booking.
